1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,075
What if sunlight switched off?
Imagine the Sun stays in place, but
suddenly stops emitting light.

2
00:00:06,075 --> 00:00:10,870
We would not notice immediately.
Light already on its way would still
travel toward Earth.

3
00:00:10,870 --> 00:00:16,185
Sunlight takes about eight minutes
to reach us. Only after that delay
would the sky change.

4
00:00:16,185 --> 00:00:21,685
In this scenario the Sun still has
its mass. Darkness alone would not
fling Earth out of its orbit.

5
00:00:21,685 --> 00:00:28,180
Earth would begin losing heat
without its usual sunlight. Cooling
and ecological effects would unfold
over time.

6
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:33,605
The lesson is to define the
question. Turning off the light and
removing the Sun are different
experiments.
